The portable C in the scenario setup-screen: what it is expected to show
otherwise than the original. A patch of harness/goldens/setup-screen.txt, see
harness/goldens.py: a line with - is the golden's, a line with + is what is
expected in its place.
Deviation: 5 of src/portable_c/DEVIATIONS.md
Why: Screen and Mouse of the setup has no Screen output: the Other options and
the Mouse options stand five rows further up, where that group was, with the
right half empty below them. The fields go to each other as they stand: right
of Screen colors is Zooming boxes; above Zooming boxes is the last line of
Screen blank delay, where the cursor is after Up, and the original's is on the
last line of Screen output; left of the line of characters is Screen colors,
where the original's cursor is on Screen blank delay; and Up twice from
Left-handed mouse is Zooming boxes, where three times is the original's Screen
output. The two steps that choose a line of Screen output are left out, the
clicks on the right half are five rows further up, and the mouse pointer with
them. The setup file that is saved has the byte of that setting as it had it,
2, where the original's has 1, Asynchronized access, and so another sum: the
file differs in those two bytes. The mouse pointer exchanges the colours of
the cell that it is on, the middle of the screen where nothing has moved it:
the lines have moved under it, and it stays

